# S0b (STOP): the BAKED serving profile of the window image (the Lever N traffic profile) on the window image WITHOUT the audits: the bytes a platform launch serves. The smoke action always passes QWEN_C2_PROFILE, so the profile
# is named here; that the image boots it by its own default with no profile set is read in SR10 (the replay sets none). READ: '[QWEN-C2] profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-traffic', admission passed with no UNQUALIFIED and no waiver,
# parser M armed; every hash EQUAL to the production reference smoke (the 32k prompts are split steps here; no card run has yet shown that the split prefill is exact (the audited exactness arms are not part of this pack), so a mismatch is a FINDING and the stop class hands the cards back). Measured basis: v579 8.9 minutes, v524 11.6.
# TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the second chained session of 2026-10-08 (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it). ORDER.txt has the order, the classes, the minutes, the boxes, the tags
# and every rule. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-11 is the window image (the Lever N traffic profile baked in as its default); tp4-serve-10 is the production base image. C2_BOX_MINUTES is the job's box:
# the workflow enforces it from inside, it never cancels a run. NO profile of this pack carries a digest or an audit (QWEN_PREFIX_DIGESTS, QWEN_PREFIX_AUDIT, the lever audits): test_tp4_session_0808b pins that.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-11
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-traffic
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_code_32k,concurrent8_code_equal
C2_BOX_MINUTES=20
